---
import Container from "@components/Container.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "@consts";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy for Boran's portfolio.">
	<Container>
		<article class="space-y-6">
			<h1 class="text-fg-bright animate text-xl font-semibold">Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="text-fg-muted animate text-xs">Last updated: March 11, 2026</p>

			<article class="animate space-y-6">
				<section class="space-y-4">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">The short version</h2>
					<p>
						I'm not interested in tracking you. This portfolio is just a place to show what I can
						do. I don't use analytics, I don't set tracking cookies, and I don't sell your data.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="space-y-4">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">The chatbot</h2>
					<p>
						The only time I see any data from you is if you talk to the AI chatbot. When you send a
						message, it travels through a Cloudflare Worker and their AI Gateway before hitting the
						Google Gemini API.
					</p>
					<p>
						Cloudflare keeps logs of these conversations for a few weeks. I use those logs to make
						sure the bot isn't crashing and to see how people are interacting with it. I don't have
						any long-term storage set up for these messages.
					</p>
					<p>
						Because I run this from Switzerland, Google's "Paid Services" terms apply to the Gemini
						API. This means Google doesn't use your prompts or the bot's answers to train their AI
						models. They might keep the data briefly to catch abuse or for legal reasons, but nobody
						is sitting there reading your chats to improve the algorithm. You can check the details
						in <a
							href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's API terms</a
						>.
					</p>
					<p>
						One heads-up: I can't delete individual messages once they've been sent. If you're not
						okay with that, it's probably best to skip the chatbot. And please, don't put anything
						sensitive or personal in there. It's an AI, after all.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="space-y-4">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">The services I use</h2>
					<p>
						If you want to dive deeper into the privacy practices of the tools powering the chatbot,
						here are their policies:
					</p>
					<ul class="list-outside list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
						<li>
							<a
								href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a
							>
						</li>
						<li>
							<a
								href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a
							>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section class="space-y-4">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Get in touch</h2>
					<p>
						Got questions? Send me an email at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.EMAIL}`}>{SITE.EMAIL}</a>.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="border-border space-y-4 border-t pt-4">
					<p class="text-fg-muted text-xs italic">
						I might update this policy occasionally. If I do, I'll change the "last updated" date at
						the top of the page.
					</p>
				</section>
			</article>
		</article>
	</Container>
</BaseLayout>
